WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.110 size:88% position:44% line:92%
- How do you balance it?

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.280 line:92%
'Cause it's hard, I get it.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.160 line:92%
Balancing a career, family, everything going on.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:04.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How do you do that?

00:00:04.993 --> 00:00:06.600 size:84% position:42% line:92%
- Well, fame is tricky.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.570 line:92%
And fame can be a very tricky thing, as you know.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.780 line:92%
As you guys can imagine, and we've experienced.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.360 line:92%
And it could be very intoxicating to people.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.880 line:92%
And I also feel with fame,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.710 line:92%
I felt early that it was really important

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.073 line:92%
to keep perspective and to understand that really fame

00:00:20.073 --> 00:00:21.640 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is like a microscope.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.750 line:92%
And it magnifies who you are as a human being

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.400 line:92%
and what you have in your DNA

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.303 line:92%
and your soul. - True colors.

00:00:26.303 --> 00:00:28.212 line:92%
- True colors, your true colors, sure.

00:00:28.212 --> 00:00:32.420 line:92%
And I think what's helped me and certainly my family

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.760 line:92%
is just remembering where I've come from

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.250 line:92%
and keeping the hard times

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.240 line:92%
that I've went through in the past.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.574 line:92%
Keep them at the forefront of my mind.

00:00:40.574 --> 00:00:41.960 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Help lead and guide me.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.800 line:92%
That way, if we're fortunate enough

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.047 line:92%
to have any bit of success, whatever it is come our way,

00:00:46.047 --> 00:00:47.960 line:92%
you take it with a grain of salt.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.600 line:92%
You're super grateful that it happens, but--

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.450 line:92%
- But it's not everything.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.270 line:92%
- It's not everything, no, not at all.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.910 line:92%
And just like that things can change.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.160 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So be super grateful.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.690 line:92%
I try and live in gratitude every day,

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.710 line:92%
and laugh things off. - [Kelly] Yeah, I actually

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.225 line:92%
have a gratitude journal. - You do?

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.991 line:92%
- Yes, 'cause somebody told me.

00:01:00.991 --> 00:01:02.360 line:92%
'Cause I try and live like that

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.790 line:92%
and my biggest fear in this industry,

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.273 line:92%
I've never said this in an interview anywhere.

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:06.953 line:92%
But I don't know why I'm saying it now.

00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:07.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
(laughing)

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:09.570 line:92%
- Talk to me. - You should be a host.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.940 line:92%
(laughing) (audience laughing)

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.700 line:92%
No, my biggest fear is becoming those people you meet

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.410 line:92%
that are so unhappy in this industry.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.527 line:92%
And I'm like, "What went wrong?

00:01:16.527 --> 00:01:17.827 line:92%
"Wait, you used to be really lovely.

00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:19.200 line:92%
"I knew you way back when."

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.410 line:92%
And it's like, what went wrong?

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.243 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And that's the thing,

00:01:21.243 --> 00:01:24.033 line:92%
I think you just lose sight of it and you chase.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.249 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And you don't enjoy.

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:27.449 line:92%
- Absolutely, and I always think.

00:01:27.449 --> 00:01:29.760 line:92%
I get asked this question often,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.657 line:92%
and I'm sure you do, too.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:34.357 line:92%
"Don't you miss the anonymity of just being able

00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:36.470 line:92%
"to go the mall, or just being able to go out?"

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.610 line:92%
'Cause that just doesn't happen anymore for me,

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:40.664 line:92%
and I say. - Just for me.

00:01:40.664 --> 00:01:44.697 line:92%
This looks a lot different in real life, Dwayne.

00:01:44.697 --> 00:01:45.670 line:92%
(laughing) (audience laughing)

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.440 line:92%
- I have put on bucket hats,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.940 line:92%
I have put on things. - [Kelly] I mean look at you.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.857 line:92%
- But I also remind myself,

00:01:53.857 --> 00:01:54.770 line:92%
"Well, what's the alternative?"

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.850 line:92%
The alternative can be I go to how things were

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.150 line:92%
when I had $7 in my pocket and that was it.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.055 line:92%
Or getting evicted. - [Kelly] Me, too.

00:02:00.055 --> 00:02:01.481 size:78% position:39% line:92%
- So I remember that.

00:02:01.481 --> 00:02:03.258 line:92%
- Running from the REPO man, I did it.

00:02:03.258 --> 00:02:04.199 line:92%
(laughing) (audience laughing)

00:02:04.199 --> 00:02:06.320 line:92%
I parked my car in my friend's apartment.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.038 line:92%
I was like, "Shoot, I don't know where it went.

00:02:08.038 --> 00:02:09.417 line:92%
"I don't know." (laughing)

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:10.617 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Somebody stole my car."

